WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.880
Kenya's court stopped a 50-bed U.S. Ebola site until the deal is disclosed. This is Omni View, episode 248. After this, arrests in Germany over an alleged synagogue plot, strikes in Gaza and a refinery fire in Bangkok. Then the India tariff argument, seabirds used a scouts, Sudan's farms, and a look at why a Russian ship hit far from the front may already have been stuck. Judge Patricia Nyoundy of Kenya's high court set on Thursday, the government broke the Constitution. Al-Jazeera reports

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.860
reports she found that Nairobi signed a deal with the United States for an Ebola quarantine

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.740
site and never showed the public the terms or asked people what they thought. Further

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.400
work stays stopped until that disclosure and that consultation happened. The beds are

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:48.860
inside Laikipia airbase near the town of Nanuki. The plan was to hold people who might have

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:54.160
been exposed, including American citizens. In July, seven American aid workers who had

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.820
been helping in the Democratic Republic of the Congo quarantined there, opposition has

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:04.000
not stayed in the courtroom. In June, police opened fire on protesters, and at least one

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.460
person was killed. The week before this ruling, hundreds marched in Nanyuki. At least two

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:15.000
people were killed, and one was wounded. This is not the first court stop. In late May, the same

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.980
court suspended construction, then found health minister Adin Duole had not obeyed. He later told

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:26.020
the judges he had ordered an immediate halt. The medical backdrop is the Bundibugio strain,

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:30.080
pain, a form of Ebola with no approved vaccine and no approved treatment.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:35.020
The World Health Organization, the United Nations Health Agency, called the outbreak

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.960
in International Public Health Emergency on May 17.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:43.980
Kenya's first imported case came in early October, a traveler from Congo by way of Uganda.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:49.540
By mid-November, the count was two deaths and seven other cases, all of those seven recovered

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.700
and no new case since October 19.

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.920
The government has not commented on Thursday's ruling.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:59.760
Both sides of the political fight accept that a site was built and that an outbreak is real.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.320
They split on whether it could go up in secret.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:08.000
Residents of Nanuki and Laikipia say the United States is parking a bowl of risk on Kenyan ground,

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:09.620
and their reason is simple.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.800
The beds are in their county and they were not shown the paper.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:20.120
Kenyan and American authorities had already restated in public that they were sticking with the plan even after the May suspension,

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:25.040
because exposed people, including Americans back from Congo, needed a place to

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.100
wait out a virus that still has no shot.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.620
Nihondi did not pick a medical winner. She said residents were left standing

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.700
outside a sealed wooden window, able to tell that decisions were happening and

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:40.600
given no way in. The court record also shows the earlier pause was not kept until

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:45.617
the minister said he had finally ordered work to stop. Germany's federal prosecutor

00:02:45.617 --> 00:02:52.037
on Thursday ordered two Iraqi citizens held, Deutscheweller reports, identified as Mustafa Al-Ar

00:02:52.037 --> 00:02:55.797
and Amir J, one taken in Heidelberg and one in Kallon.

00:02:56.677 --> 00:03:00.857
Prosecutors called them strongly suspected members of a domestic terrorist organization.

00:03:01.437 --> 00:03:07.197
More than 250 officers were in the operation, and searches at 17 sites across three states

00:03:07.197 --> 00:03:08.057
were still underway.

00:03:08.677 --> 00:03:13.937
The case they described runs through a man in the United States, Muhammad al-Sadi, accused

00:03:13.937 --> 00:03:18.717
of building a group known as Ha'i, Harakat Ashab al-Yamin al-Islamiyah.

00:03:19.357 --> 00:03:24.057
Prosecutors say that group carried out attacks on American, Israeli, and Jewish institutions

00:03:24.057 --> 00:03:27.677
in Europe from March, after Donald Trump's war with Iran began.

00:03:28.317 --> 00:03:33.777
They say Mustafa and al-Sadi then set up a separate organization at the end of 2025 to

00:03:33.777 --> 00:03:38.737
prepare more attacks in Germany and Europe, raised money, and recruited people for bombings.

00:03:38.737 --> 00:03:41.697
On two nights late in March, prosecutors wrote,

00:03:42.217 --> 00:03:44.897
Unknown assailants went, presumably carrying explosives,

00:03:45.397 --> 00:03:48.697
towards synagogues in Cologne and in one other European city.

00:03:49.237 --> 00:03:50.637
The plan was not carried out.

00:03:51.057 --> 00:03:52.497
Why it stopped is still unknown.

00:03:53.097 --> 00:03:57.817
The tip, they said, came from the BFV, Germany's domestic intelligence agency.

00:03:58.337 --> 00:04:03.157
The two men were due before judges later Thursday, so the court could decide investigative detention,

00:04:03.677 --> 00:04:04.897
which is pretrial jail.

00:04:05.477 --> 00:04:06.977
A third person is still wanted.

00:04:06.977 --> 00:04:10.077
This report carries the prosecution's account only.

00:04:10.577 --> 00:04:15.377
The accused have no quoted answer in it, and Deutschewella marks the story as still developing.

00:04:15.917 --> 00:04:19.597
Watch whether those judges ordered the two men kept an investigative detention.

00:04:20.622 --> 00:04:26.082
Israeli attacks killed at least eight Palestinians across Gaza on Thursday, Al-Jazeera reports,

00:04:26.622 --> 00:04:32.082
and the dead include Khaled Abu Nada, Under Secretary of Gaza's Education Ministry, and

00:04:32.082 --> 00:04:32.562
his wife.

00:04:32.562 --> 00:04:38.062
Medics at Al-Oxam martyrs hospital in western deer al-Bala set an airstrike killed the couple

00:04:38.062 --> 00:04:40.882
and wounded six others, several of them critically.

00:04:41.582 --> 00:04:47.262
Correspondent Ashraf Abu Amra set Apache helicopters fired two missiles, one after the other at

00:04:47.262 --> 00:04:52.482
a residential apartment during dawn prayers, in a district packed with tents of displaced families.

00:04:53.042 --> 00:04:58.542
In the north, Al-Shifa hospital set a drone hit a group in Shati refugee camp, killing three

00:04:58.542 --> 00:04:59.542
and wounding four.

00:04:59.542 --> 00:05:05.562
a separate strike on the Tufa neighborhood killed three. Another drone attack on NASA wounded

00:05:05.562 --> 00:05:11.422
several people. A ceasefire has been in effect since last October. The argument is about the job

00:05:11.422 --> 00:05:16.782
title and about what a strike in a ceasefire is doing. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:21.902
Defense Minister Israel Katz said Abu Nada was a Hamas figure in charge of the group's economy

00:05:21.902 --> 00:05:29.522
and education portfolios. So the strike on their account hit Hamas administration rather than a

00:05:29.522 --> 00:05:33.982
Gaza's interior ministry says Israel is trying to spread chaos by killing security and

00:05:33.982 --> 00:05:34.802
police commanders.

00:05:35.162 --> 00:05:37.722
That charge follows two other killings this week.

00:05:38.262 --> 00:05:43.462
Muhammad Abu Al-Uf, internal security chief for northern Gaza, died early Wednesday with

00:05:43.462 --> 00:05:48.902
his wife and two daughters, and Naim Abu Nahul, the internal security director, was killed

00:05:48.902 --> 00:05:49.562
the day before.

00:05:50.202 --> 00:05:55.482
Health ministry spokesperson Zahar Al-Wahidi told Al-Jazirah that Israeli attacks since the cease

00:05:55.482 --> 00:06:01.542
fire have killed more than 1,600 Palestinians, 130 of them this month, and wounded more than

00:06:01.542 --> 00:06:07.262
6,000. He called it a systematic hit on every pillar of life in the strip. The Ministry's

00:06:07.262 --> 00:06:14.402
count since October 2023 is 74,746 killed. Neither side grants the other's description

00:06:14.402 --> 00:06:20.864
of Abu Nada, an explosion in fire at Bangchak Corporation's Prokhanong Oil Facility in Eastern

00:06:20.864 --> 00:06:26.424
Bangkok injured at least seven people on Thursday. Four of them seriously, Al-Jazeera reports,

00:06:27.044 --> 00:06:31.784
citing the city's Arawan Emergency Center. The company said it shut every production unit,

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:37.044
contained the blaze, and got the situation under control. The bang-nut district office told

00:06:37.044 --> 00:06:42.784
anyone nearby to leave immediately and said investigators do not yet know the cause. A citywide

00:06:42.784 --> 00:06:47.044
phone alert repeated that the fire was under control and told people to stay away.

00:06:47.804 --> 00:06:53.084
Bangchak's own description of the plant puts maximum capacity at 120,000 barrels a day.

00:06:53.624 --> 00:06:58.664
It feeds not only Bangkok, but a large share of the oil imports for Central Thailand, and

00:06:58.664 --> 00:06:59.924
it sits near the main port.

00:07:00.744 --> 00:07:05.024
Correspondent Tony Chang said the blast was heard around three in the afternoon local time,

00:07:05.484 --> 00:07:08.464
and that the highway and most major routes in the area stayed open.

00:07:09.044 --> 00:07:14.164
Prime Minister Anutin Charne Virakul said he was watching, that the fire appeared under control,

00:07:14.164 --> 00:07:17.184
and that it did not seem to be in the main production area.

00:07:17.664 --> 00:07:19.044
He gave no further detail.

00:07:19.624 --> 00:07:24.504
The same refinery blew up in July 2012 when it was still called Bangchak Petroleum.

00:07:25.124 --> 00:07:28.664
That fire was huge and by the reports then hurt no one.

00:07:29.204 --> 00:07:33.684
People asked at the time why a plant that large stood in what is now a residential district.

00:07:34.444 --> 00:07:38.264
Chang noted other industrial accidents in the area over the past couple of years.

00:07:38.744 --> 00:07:42.424
How much of the plant Thursday's fire actually ruined is not yet public.

00:07:42.424 --> 00:07:48.456
A new paper from the USTR, the Office of the United States Trade Representative, puts

00:07:48.456 --> 00:07:52.116
American tariffs on India back where they were when the trade talks started.

00:07:52.576 --> 00:07:56.916
That is the Hindus report, and the experts at sites say the move is not a substantial

00:07:56.916 --> 00:07:59.656
threat, so India should not hurry into a deal.

00:08:00.456 --> 00:08:05.276
Deutschewella adds that New Delhi has denied a U.S. claim that Indian policy creates too much

00:08:05.276 --> 00:08:10.256
factory capacity and has told Washington to settle the terrified inside the negotiations.

00:08:10.836 --> 00:08:15.436
Reuters describes President Donald Trump's new tariffs as a tool to pull global trade

00:08:15.436 --> 00:08:16.436
out of China's grip.

00:08:16.936 --> 00:08:22.196
Start with India's own framing, the government and the experts the Hindu summarizes, treat

00:08:22.196 --> 00:08:27.396
this text as a return to the opening bid, not a gun to the head, and they reject the idea

00:08:27.396 --> 00:08:30.356
that Indian policy is flooding the world with surplus goods.

00:08:31.136 --> 00:08:36.016
Washington's framing, as Reuters states the aim, is not really about that India paper alone.

00:08:36.016 --> 00:08:42.216
tariffs are there to loosen China's hold on trade, which puts India's terms inside a wider contest.

00:08:42.756 --> 00:08:48.815
Nothing in these reports shows either capital-conceiting a point. Researchers are strapping sea birds with

00:08:48.815 --> 00:08:55.175
GPS units, satellite trackers, and with microphones, the New York Times reports, so the birds can lead

00:08:55.175 --> 00:09:00.275
them to fishing boats that sail with their tracking signals off. Those signals are how satellites usually

00:09:00.275 --> 00:09:06.135
see a vessel. Switch the box off and the boat disappears from that map. A bird that follows it can

00:09:06.135 --> 00:09:11.035
still log the track and the sound. The piece is about the method. It does not name a fleet,

00:09:11.315 --> 00:09:16.931
a fine, or a government that has acted on what the birds found. Attacks on electricity lines

00:09:16.931 --> 00:09:21.491
and a drought are hitting Sudan's harvests at the same time. Al Jazeera reports,

00:09:22.191 --> 00:09:27.291
and millions of people are left without water. Farmers are the ones who season depends on both the

00:09:27.291 --> 00:09:32.471
grid and the rain. The report puts the war damage and the dry weather on the same fields.

00:09:32.471 --> 00:09:37.571
It does not name a repair crew, a relief shipment, or a ceasefire clause that would turn the

00:09:37.571 --> 00:09:38.391
power back on.

00:09:39.361 --> 00:09:43.801
In brief, a Russian-installed official said a Ukrainian drone strike killed five people

00:09:43.801 --> 00:09:50.761
and wounded three in Vesia, in occupied Zaporizia, while Kiev mayor Vitaly Klitschko said ballistic

00:09:50.761 --> 00:09:53.241
missiles hit a shopping center and two other buildings.

00:09:53.881 --> 00:09:58.321
Fighting in eastern Congo is pushing out health workers and civilians as authorities face

00:09:58.321 --> 00:10:04.501
the country's worst Ebola outbreak with cases past 12,000. The New York Times reports dozens

00:10:04.501 --> 00:10:09.021
of Brazilians were sent to Russia's front with little training after recruiters promised

00:10:09.021 --> 00:10:14.761
salaries the men say never came. Police in Bangladesh fired tear gas to break up fresh garment

00:10:14.761 --> 00:10:20.623
worker protests after a wage rise that did not end the dispute. To really understand a blast

00:10:20.623 --> 00:10:25.743
on a Russian ship far from Ukraine, separate a random spillover from a ship that geography

00:10:25.743 --> 00:10:30.583
he already trapped. It is easy to hear a hit in the Baltic or the Mediterranean as the

00:10:30.583 --> 00:10:35.983
land war simply leaking into NATO seas. Deutsche Welle's account of those operations is more

00:10:35.983 --> 00:10:41.143
precise than that. Russia's Baltic shoreline is a thin strip between Finland and Estonia.

00:10:41.783 --> 00:10:46.343
Through it, Moscow supplies Kaliningrad, a piece of Russia cut off from the mainland,

00:10:46.823 --> 00:10:52.263
and ships oil out on a shadow fleet of tankers. Ukraine had already struck oil terminals on that

00:10:52.263 --> 00:10:56.023
same coast, at Ust Luga and Primorsk near St. Petersburg.

00:10:56.743 --> 00:11:01.363
A corvette that belonged to the Black Sea fleet could not go home, because Turkey has closed

00:11:01.363 --> 00:11:06.023
the Bosporus and the Dardanelles, the two straits between the Black Sea and the Mediterranean,

00:11:06.643 --> 00:11:09.963
so the warship was escorting cargo ships in the Mediterranean instead.

00:11:10.663 --> 00:11:16.043
Elizabeth Braw of the Atlantic Council told Deutschewella, this is not a sweep of every tanker selling

00:11:16.043 --> 00:11:17.303
oil above a price cap.

00:11:17.303 --> 00:11:23.083
The cargo ship Sparta 2 struck off Finland, was suspected of hauling military equipment.

00:11:23.643 --> 00:11:24.843
Moscow denies that.

00:11:25.263 --> 00:11:30.383
What Kiev is demonstrating, she said, is that it can find those ships in whatever water they occupy.

00:11:30.943 --> 00:11:33.703
The stated military aim is to snap supply lines.

00:11:34.323 --> 00:11:39.243
Experts and politicians also hear a political message to Western allies ahead of any peace talks.

00:11:39.943 --> 00:11:45.123
This is not the first far-strike. Ukraine has hit an oil refinery in Omsk in Siberia,

00:11:45.123 --> 00:11:49.783
Russia, and before December 2024, Russian military sites in Syria.

00:11:50.303 --> 00:11:55.083
Next time a report names a ship a long way from the front, check which label it actually

00:11:55.083 --> 00:12:01.263
earns, warship, alleged arms cargo, or shadow fleet tanker, and whether Moscow denies what

00:12:01.263 --> 00:12:02.463
was said to be in the hold.

00:12:03.368 --> 00:12:07.928
A court order, a charge sheet, and a minister's sentence are not the same kind of fact.

00:12:08.448 --> 00:12:13.108
One you can read as a ruling, one is still an allegation, and one is an official summary

00:12:13.108 --> 00:12:14.528
of a file you have not seen.

00:12:14.528 --> 00:12:21.808
When two governments name the same dead man in opposite ways, the document each will publish matters more than a blend of both.

00:12:22.268 --> 00:12:26.288
